    "Scaling arguments explain enormous amounts of biology and engineering with no detailed model: area goes as length squared and volume as length cubed, so bone stress grows with size, small things dry fast, and designs cannot simply be scaled up.",
    "Fermi estimation decomposes an unknown into factors you can each bound, relies on independent errors partially cancelling, and ends in a quoted range plus an independent cross-check.",
